<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hentschel, Glimm, Glazier & Newman (2004) Proc. R. Soc. B / Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. multiscale TGF-beta / FGF-inhibitor reaction-diffusion and fibronectin haptotaxis PDE in developing Gallus gallus limb bud, coupled to a Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg cellular Potts cell lattice — Code-to-model traceability: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-95) maps the GGH module to Graner & Glazier (1992), Glazier & Graner (1993), Savill & Hogeweg (1997), Chaturvedi (2005) and Tapia & D'Souza (2011) and names the volume-filling source; the function docstring (L698-724) states the Hamiltonian, the copy energy, the acceptance rule, the coupling laws and the parallel approximation; inline comments mark the three coupling steps (L790, L796, L800); the math KG (`hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.yaml`) registers 5 laws with Lean theorem names, Lean loci and corrected code loci. Deductions: the per-zone dt multipliers (L473), the 3.75 and 0.40 factors and the 180-step haptotaxis loop have no equation citation (-4); the CPM GIF frame step/time mapping (1 MCS = dt_F) is a modelling choice stated only in the JSON (-2); the stale \"8-check\" wording is gone but Law 2/3 code loci span whole sections rather than equations (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py L473–L473: dt_z per-zone multipliers (3.2 / 1.25 / 0.85) uncited <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L473-L473>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hentschel, Glimm, Glazier & Newman (2004) Proc. R. Soc. B / Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. multiscale TGF-beta / FGF-inhibitor reaction-diffusion and fibronectin haptotaxis PDE in developing Gallus gallus limb bud, coupled to a Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg cellular Potts cell lattice — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: the Hentschel et al. (2004) dispersion (L185-266) and the 4-field PDE structure in 1D (L271-418), 2D wing (L421-536) and periodic micromass (L539-644) are the published equations; the new GGH module (L678-862) is a correct Graner-Glazier Hamiltonian (adhesion L811-815, volume L816-817, Savill-Hogeweg haptotaxis L818-819, Metropolis L820) coupled to the continuum through the PDE's own Hill switch (L790-793) and a two-way fibronectin law (L796-798), with the adhesion energy exact within each stride-3 sub-sweep; the micromass solver now uses the Hillen-Painter volume-filling form (L605-606) and reaches a resolved solution (clip fraction 0.000). Deductions: the 1D haptotaxis step (L353-365) collapses R(x) onto the two clip levels for fa = 11 and 18 (clip_fraction_R = 1.00; 0.52 at fa = 6) and the 2D wing step (L495-512) pins 19.3 % of R(x, z), so the reported condensation amplitudes, std(R) and the F-R correlation r = 0.9997 are set by np.clip, not by the PDE (-10); the 1D and 2D solvers also carry uncited factors 3.75 * D_R (L335) and 0.40 (L361) and per-zone dt multipliers (L473) that are tuning, not Hentschel (2004) parameters (-4); the GGH volume term uses sub-sweep-stale volumes (L816-817), an acknowledged parallel-CPM approximation never validated against a sequential update (-3); Kiskowski et al. (2004) itself is not a CPM, so the \"as in Kiskowski\" coupling is a Chaturvedi-style realisation (disclosed, -2); lambda_V = 6 departs from the Graner-Glazier lambda = 1 for cell survival (disclosed in the JSON, -1); the stylopod condensation exists only in the collapsed continuum, not in the discrete model (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py L353–L365: 1D haptotaxis step without volume filling and with an uncited 0.40 divergence factor; clip_fraction_R = 1.00 for fa = 11 and 18 — condensation amplitudes are clip-determined <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L353-L365>",
        "2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py L495–L512: 2D wing haptotaxis loop (180 explicit steps, denom_R without the 3.75 factor); 19.3 % of R(x, z) pinned at the clip bounds, digit condensations are single-pixel lines (Panel B) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L495-L512>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hentschel, Glimm, Glazier & Newman (2004) Proc. R. Soc. B / Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. multiscale TGF-beta / FGF-inhibitor reaction-diffusion and fibronectin haptotaxis PDE in developing Gallus gallus limb bud, coupled to a Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg cellular Potts cell lattice — Morphometric validation: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: `measure_morphoeval()` (L1457-1612) now returns 14 measurements, every one with a reference value; the 6 new ones quantify the discrete-continuum parity (condensation index 1.355 vs continuum 1.514; heterotypic fraction 0.293 vs ablation 0.514; r(R2 disc, R2 cont) = 0.918 vs ablation 0.800; GGH wing total 5 vs 6) and add two honest failing diagnostics (2D wing clip fraction 0.193 vs 0; resolved micromass 8 vs 6 islands). Deductions: the GGH references are internal — the continuum ratio, the ablation value, an adopted r >= 0.9 threshold and the +TGF-beta2 island count — because Kiskowski (2004) / Glazier & Graner (1993) values were not extracted (-8); the Pass 2 measurements 1-7 still report counts and a F-R correlation computed on clip-collapsed fields without flagging them individually (-5); the micromass area fractions (0.21 / 0.21) are no longer compared with the dataset's 25-30 % vs 45-55 % Miura & Shiota ranges because the model cannot reproduce them (-4); no uncertainty (seed replicates) on any GGH metric (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
