<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hentschel, Glimm, Glazier & Newman (2004) Proc. R. Soc. B / Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. multiscale TGF-beta / FGF-inhibitor reaction-diffusion and fibronectin haptotaxis PDE in developing Gallus gallus limb bud, coupled to a Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg cellular Potts cell lattice — MorphoEval overall 82.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) post-remediation evaluation of `2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py` (overall weighted score 82.6 / 100, down 10.0 points from 92.6 in Pass 2). The single Pass 2 remediation item is closed: Section 3b implements a Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg cellular Potts lattice (Graner-Glazier contact energies 14/2/11/16, T = 10, lambda_V = 6, Savill-Hogeweg haptotaxis mu_F = 10, Metropolis acceptance, checkerboard-parallel sweeps) coupled to the continuum through the PDE's own Hill switch for the R1 -> R2 state and a two-way cell-deposited fibronectin field. On the x3-upsampled WT micromass prepattern the four GGH regimes order as WT 1.355 > DA-only 1.204 > haptotaxis-only 1.078 > full ablation 0.969 in condensation index (continuum 1.514), the heterotypic boundary fraction falls from 0.514 (ablation) to 0.293 (WT), the discrete R2 density correlates with the continuum R_2 at r = 0.918 (ablation 0.800), all 1296 cells survive, and on the 2D wing bud the lattice forms [0, 2, 3] discrete condensations against the continuum [1, 2, 3]. The score falls because Pass 3 also found that the Pass 2 continuum fields were chemotactically collapsed: the micromass \"spots vs stripes\" contrast (19.8 % vs 44.8 %) was an artefact of thresholding a field with 24 % of pixels pinned at the clip bounds (now fixed with volume-filling haptotaxis; both regimes are labyrinthine), and the 1D stage (100 % pinned at fa = 11, 18) and 2D wing (19.3 % pinned) solvers still are — counts hold, amplitudes do not. Lean Laws 4-5 are machine-checked (0 sorrys); the dataset gains a SHA-256-pinned GGH parameter table and 5 DOIs. Overall 82.6/100 (faithfulness 78.6, reproducibility 92.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 58b898c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 78, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/tgfb_fibronectin_limb_comparison.png: rendered output of 2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py at 58b898c, image/png, 853011 B, 2343×1960 px, artifact_sha256 f0533eb3a15144051abc88f164c957218c60b35cd76f3088949b7fd3d12be3e2 (sha256 f0533eb3a15144051abc88f164c957218c60b35cd76f3088949b7fd3d12be3e2), spec_fingerprint 25a54774cc76963703511eae8cb9dc8b8fea2169f1c58b48380f2c9d1c3fe31f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 25a54774cc76963703511eae8cb9dc8b8fea2169f1c58b48380f2c9d1c3fe31f; artifact_sha256: f0533eb3a15144051abc88f164c957218c60b35cd76f3088949b7fd3d12be3e2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/tgfb_fibronectin_limb/chick_limb_chondrogenesis_specimen.jpg=771e26f9fe8c813d..., datasets/tgfb_fibronectin_limb/kiskowski_ggh_cpm_reference.json=a7d13368e41d762a..., datasets/tgfb_fibronectin_limb/scout_manifest.json=c810bd77e66557c8..., datasets/tgfb_fibronectin_limb/tgfb_fibronectin_limb_reference.json=33d554e44b712e2b...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Hentschel et al. (2004): a 4-field TGF-beta activator / FGF-dependent inhibitor / fibronectin / mesenchymal-cell-density reaction-diffusion-haptotaxis system whose AER-FGF-modulated unstable wavenumber increases proximodistally, giving 1 -> 2 -> 3 skeletal elements | Kiskowski et al. (2004): discrete cells on a lattice with a continuous activator/inhibitor prepattern, activated cells deposit fibronectin and bind to it, producing autonomous condensations; Chaturvedi et al. (2005): the same scheme realised in a GGH cellular Potts framework (CompuCell) | Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993): differential adhesion with J_dd < J_ld < J_ll < J_cM at T = 10 sorts cells; heterotypic boundary length decreases | Miura & Shiota (2000): exogenous TGF-beta2 fuses micromass condensations into bar-like patterns; anti-fibronectin treatment blocks condensation; reconstructed_in_script: Linear dispersion of the activator/inhibitor subsystem, 1D and 2D (x, z) pseudo-spectral IMEX integration of the 4-field system with zero-flux boundaries, 2D periodic micromass morphospace with volume-filling haptotaxis, dual negative controls, a GGH cellular Potts lattice coupled through the PDE's Hill switch and a two-way fibronectin field, four GGH regimes plus a wing-bud GGH run, specimen segmentation of a Gallus wing, 14 measurements, 5 Lean 4 theorems; transfer_boundary: Kiskowski et al. (2004) is a lattice-cell / biased-random-walk model, not a cellular Potts model; the GGH realisation follows Chaturvedi et al. (2005), as the Pass 2 remediation item requested, and the dataset JSON says so | The 1D stage and 2D wing continuum solutions are chemotactically collapsed (clip_fraction_R = 1.00 at fa = 11, 18; 0.52 at fa = 6; 0.193 in 2D): condensation counts are reproduced but amplitudes, std(R) and F-R correlations are clip-determined | GGH references are internal (continuum ratio, ablation value, adopted thresholds) because the cited discrete-model papers do not report the metrics used here; does_not_claim: A hexagonal nodular-spot micromass regime (both resolved continuum regimes are labyrinthine), a discrete stylopod condensation (GGH gives [0, 2, 3]), quantitative agreement with Kiskowski et al. (2004) condensation sizes, a sequential (exact-volume) cellular Potts update, 3D geometry, limb outgrowth, or cell division." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py:1231-1258 — Panel G's chi_F sweep plots std(R) of clip-collapsed 1D fields (plateau 0.76 = clip ceiling). Replace with a resolved amplitude metric once item 1 lands, and add a rendered mu_F sweep (0, 5, 10, 25) for the GGH lattice showing the fingering regime disclosed in the JSON.",
        "remediation needed: 2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py:1551-1611 — measurements 9-14 use internal references (continuum condensation index, ablation heterotypic fraction, an adopted r >= 0.9 threshold, the +TGF-beta2 island count). Extract quantitative anchors from Kiskowski et al. (2004) (condensation number/size vs cell density, Figs. 4-7) and Glazier & Graner (1993) (boundary-length decay) and add seed-replicate uncertainty to each GGH metric.",
        "remediation needed: 2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py:353-365 and 335 — the 1D haptotaxis step pins 100 % of R(x) at the clip bounds for fa = 11 and 18 (52 % at fa = 6; `clip_fraction_R`), so every reported amplitude, std(R) and F-R correlation is clip-determined. Apply the volume-filling sensitivity already used at L605-606 (or a semi-implicit haptotaxis step with a CFL-limited dt) and re-tune so that the stylopod m = 1 condensation survives (at R_max = 2 it vanishes: std(R) = 0.017, 0 peaks) — without re-tuning, assert clip_fraction_R < 0.01 in check 3.",
        "remediation needed: 2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py:495-512 — the 2D wing haptotaxis loop (explicit flux, denom_R without the 3.75 factor, 180 steps) pins 19.3 % of R(x, z) and renders digits as single-pixel lines in Panel B; stabilise it the same way and replace `_count_compartment_condensations` thresholds (L514-519) with widths measured on the resolved field compared to the specimen bone widths of Panel F.",
        "remediation needed: 2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py:539-644 — with the resolved solver both micromass regimes are labyrinthine (8 vs 6 islands, 0.21 area each), so the Miura & Shiota (2000) nodular-island (25-30 %) vs bar (45-55 %) phenotype recorded in `tgfb_fibronectin_limb_reference.json` is not reproduced; a true spot regime needs the activator kinetics in the hexagon-selecting range (quadratic term dominant near onset) rather than the current threshold shift s_TGFb = -1.10 (L635-637). Implement, then restore the area-fraction comparison to the dataset ranges.",
        "remediation needed: 2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py:816-817 and 770 — the checkerboard-parallel sweep evaluates the volume term with sub-sweep-stale cell volumes; validate against a sequential Metropolis update on a small lattice (volume distribution and energy parity) or accept at most one copy per cell per sub-sweep.",
        "remediation needed: 2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py:913-949 — the GGH wing-bud count is taken from the R2-cell density, which follows the prepattern (the full ablation also gives [0, 2, 3]); and the stylopod forms no discrete condensation because c_a max = 0.35 < K_a = 0.60 (L790-793). Count condensations from the occupancy density (behaviour- dependent) and either make the R1 -> R2 switch graded/probabilistic (matching the continuum R_2 = R Hill(c_a) mass) or raise the stylopod activator so the discrete model reproduces 1 + 2 + 3." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.26e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hentschel, Glimm, Glazier & Newman (2004) Proc. R. Soc. B / Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. multiscale TGF-beta / FGF-inhibitor reaction-diffusion and fibronectin haptotaxis PDE in developing Gallus gallus limb bud, coupled to a Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg cellular Potts cell lattice — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: the FGF zonation sweep (L955-995) still produces [1, 2, 3, 4]; the four GGH regimes (L865-910) form a genuine 2 x 2 ablation (differential adhesion x haptotaxis) whose condensation index orders monotonically WT > DA-only > haptotaxis-only > ablation and whose heterotypic fraction drops only when differential adhesion is on; new CLI flags `--cpm-mcs`, `--cpm-wing-mcs`, `--mu-F`, `--J-R2R2` (L1737-1740) are resolved at call time (L725-732). Deductions: the Panel G chi_F sweep (L1231-1258) reports std(R) on clip-collapsed fields, so its plateau at 0.76 is the clip ceiling, not a haptotaxis response (-6); the GGH wing-bud count is prepattern-determined — the full ablation also yields [0, 2, 3] (L913-949), so that panel does not test cell behaviour (-4); haptotaxis adds only +0.15 to the condensation index and mu_F was tuned by hand to 10 because mu_F >= 25 fingers cells across the Hill boundary (disclosed in the JSON) — no mu_F sweep is rendered (-4); no T or lambda_V sweep (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py L1231–L1258: Panel G chi_F sweep uses std(R) of clip-collapsed 1D fields (clip fraction 1.00 at fa = 11) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L1231-L1258>",
        "2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py L913–L949: run_cpm_wing_bud_coupling counts peaks of the R2 density; ablation gives the same [0, 2, 3] (prepattern-determined) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L913-L949>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

