<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Equal-Diffusion (D_a = D_i) & Anti-Fibronectin No-Haptotaxis (chi_F = 0) Negative Controls" ;
    dct:description "Proves that equal morphogen diffusivities abolish the TGF-beta chemical prepattern and that blocking fibronectin haptotaxis (χ_F = 0, e.g. anti-fibronectin antibody or RGD peptide) abolishes mesenchymal cell condensation | Variables: c_a: activator TGF-beta concentration; c_i: FGF-dependent inhibitor concentration; R: mesenchymal cell density; χ_F: fibronectin haptotactic sensitivity; D_R: cell random motility" ;
    dct:source "Hentschel, Glimm, Glazier & Newman (2004) Proc. R. Soc. B 271(1549):1713-1722 Eqs. (2.1)-(3.6); Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. 271(2):372-387" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L185-L266>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_014_tgfb_fibronectin_limb.lean#L21-L55> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def tgfb_modal_trace_eq_diff (tr_J0 Dq : Int) : Int := tr_J0 - 2 * Dq
def tgfb_modal_det_eq_diff (det_J0 neg_tr_Dq Dq_sq : Int) : Int :=
  det_J0 + neg_tr_Dq + Dq_sq
def sigma_R_no_hapto (D_R_q r_R : Int) : Int := -D_R_q - r_R
theorem hentschel_tgfb_inhibitor_haptotaxis_stability_controls
    (tr_J0 det_J0 Dq neg_tr_Dq Dq_sq D_R_q r_R : Int)
    (htr : tr_J0 < 0) (hdet : det_J0 > 0)
    (hDq : Dq ≥ 0) (hterm : neg_tr_Dq ≥ 0) (hsq : Dq_sq ≥ 0)
    (hDR : D_R_q ≥ 0) (hr : r_R > 0) :
    tgfb_modal_trace_eq_diff tr_J0 Dq < 0 ∧
    tgfb_modal_det_eq_diff det_J0 neg_tr_Dq Dq_sq > 0 ∧
    sigma_R_no_hapto D_R_q r_R < 0 := by
  unfold tgfb_modal_trace_eq_diff tgfb_modal_det_eq_diff sigma_R_no_hapto; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "tr(J_0) < 0 ∧ det(J_0) > 0 ∧ D_a = D_i = D ≥ 1 ∧ χ_F = 0 ⟹ ∀ q = k^2 ≥ 0, tr(J_k) < 0 ∧ det(J_k) > 0 ∧ σ_R(q; χ_F=0) = -D_R q - r_R < 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/aama.2001.0721>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0237>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2010.12.011>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.03.038>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2005.0033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2004.2772>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1752-0509-1-16> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Multiscale Reactor-Mechanochemical Limb" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_014.sigma_R_no_hapto" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_014.hentschel_tgfb_inhibitor_haptotaxis_stability_controls" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "AER-FGF Zonation & Proximodistal 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 Skeletal Mode Transition" ;
    dct:description "Proves that proximodistal AER-FGF zonation monotonically increases the unstable anteroposterior wavenumber across stylopod (m=1 humerus), zeugopod (m=2 radius+ulna), chick wing autopod (m=3 digits II-IV), and hindlimb/exogenous-TGF-beta autopod (m=4 digits I-IV) | Variables: c_FGF(z): distal AER fibroblast growth factor concentration; f_a(c_FGF) ∈ {3, 6, 11, 18}: FGF-modulated TGF-beta self-activation rate; m ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4}: anteroposterior skeletal condensation count" ;
    dct:source "Hentschel, Glimm, Glazier & Newman (2004) Proc. R. Soc. B 271(1549):1713-1722 Eqs. (3.1)-(3.12) & Figs. 2-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L271-L536>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_014_tgfb_fibronectin_limb.lean#L62-L96> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def hentschel_trace_J0 (fa : Int) : Int := fa - 200
def hentschel_mode_sq (fa : Int) : Int := fa - 2
theorem hentschel_fgf_zonation_proximodistal_mode_transition (fa1 fa2 : Int)
    (h12 : fa1 < fa2) (h2 : fa2 < 200) :
    hentschel_mode_sq fa1 < hentschel_mode_sq fa2 ∧
    hentschel_trace_J0 fa2 < 0 ∧
    hentschel_mode_sq 3 = 1 * 1 ∧
    hentschel_mode_sq 6 = 2 * 2 ∧
    hentschel_mode_sq 11 = 3 * 3 ∧
    hentschel_mode_sq 18 = 4 * 4 := by
  unfold hentschel_mode_sq hentschel_trace_J0; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "∂_t c_a = f_a(c_FGF) c_a + f_i c_i - c_a^3 + D_a ∇^2 c_a;  m^2(f_a) = (D_i f_a + D_a g_i) / (2 D_a D_i) = f_a - 2 ∈ {1^2, 2^2, 3^2, 4^2}" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/aama.2001.0721>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0237>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2010.12.011>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.03.038>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2005.0033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2004.2772>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1752-0509-1-16> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Multiscale Reactor-Mechanochemical Limb" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_014.hentschel_mode_sq" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_014.hentschel_fgf_zonation_proximodistal_mode_transition" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Fibronectin Haptotactic Positive-Feedback Amplification & Micromass Spot/Stripe Morphospace" ;
    dct:description "Proves that positive feedback between TGF-beta-stimulated fibronectin secretion and upward mesenchymal haptotaxis amplifies prechondrogenic cell condensations above random cell diffusion and governs the 2D micromass nodular-spot vs labyrinthine-stripe morphospace | Variables: F(x,z,t): extracellular matrix fibronectin concentration; R_2(c_a,R): FGF/TGF-beta-differentiated prechondrogenic cell density; χ_F S_F: effective haptotactic sensitivity" ;
    dct:source "Hentschel et al. (2004) Proc. R. Soc. B 271:1713-1722 Eqs. (2.4)-(2.9); Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. 271:372-387; Miura & Shiota (2000) Dev. Dyn. 217:241-249" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L271-L644>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_014_tgfb_fibronectin_limb.lean#L103-L130> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def hapto_net_flux (chi_F_SF D_R q : Int) : Int := (chi_F_SF - D_R) * q
theorem hentschel_kiskowski_fibronectin_haptotaxis_amplification
    (chi_F_SF D_R q : Int)
    (hchi : chi_F_SF > D_R) (hDR : D_R ≥ 0) (hq : q ≥ 1) :
    hapto_net_flux chi_F_SF D_R q > 0 ∧
    hapto_net_flux 0 D_R q ≤ 0 ∧
    hapto_net_flux chi_F_SF D_R q > hapto_net_flux 0 D_R q := by
  unfold hapto_net_flux
  have hdiff : chi_F_SF - D_R ≥ 1 := by omega
  have hpos : (chi_F_SF - D_R) * q ≥ 1 * 1 := Int.mul_le_mul hdiff hq (by omega) (by omega)
  have hneg : (0 - D_R) * q ≤ 0 := Int.mul_nonpos_of_nonpos_of_nonneg (by omega) (by omega)
  omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "∂_t F = k_F c_a^+ R_2 - γ_F F,  ∂_t R = D_R ∇^2 R - χ_F ∇·(R ∇F) + r_R R(1 - R);  J_hapto(q) = (χ_F S_F - D_R) q > 0 for χ_F S_F > D_R" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/aama.2001.0721>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0237>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2010.12.011>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.03.038>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2005.0033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2004.2772>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1752-0509-1-16> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Multiscale Reactor-Mechanochemical Limb" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_014.hapto_net_flux" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_014.hentschel_kiskowski_fibronectin_haptotaxis_amplification" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg Differential-Adhesion Sorting Condition (Pass 3 discrete cell lattice)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that the Graner-Glazier contact energies give a positive heterotypic surface tension so R2 prechondrogenic cells sort into compact condensations inside the continuum TGF-beta prepattern, and that the no-differential-adhesion ablation (equal J) removes the sorting drive — the mechanism behind the WT > DA-only > haptotaxis-only > ablation condensation-index ordering and the WT < ablation heterotypic boundary fraction in simulate_ggh_cellular_potts_condensation | Variables: σ_i: cell index at lattice site i; τ: cell type (R1 mesenchyme, R2 TGF-beta-activated prechondrogenic, M medium); J_ll = J_R1R1 = 14, J_dd = J_R2R2 = 2, J_ld = J_R1R2 = 11, J_cM = 16 (Graner & Glazier 1992); λ_V = 6 volume-constraint stiffness; V_T = 25 px target cell area" ;
    dct:source "Graner F, Glazier JA (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 69(13):2013-2016 doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013; Glazier JA, Graner F (1993) Phys. Rev. E 47(3):2128-2154 doi:10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128; Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. 271:372-387; Chaturvedi et al. (2005) J. R. Soc. Interface 2:237-253" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L649-L862>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_014_tgfb_fibronectin_limb.lean#L131-L163> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ggh_hetero_surface_tension2 (J_ll J_dd J_ld : Int) : Int := 2 * J_ld - J_ll - J_dd
def ggh_sorting_swap_dH (J_ll J_dd J_ld : Int) : Int := (J_ll + J_dd) - 2 * J_ld
theorem ggh_differential_adhesion_sorting_condition (J_ll J_dd J_ld J : Int)
    (hsort : 2 * J_ld > J_ll + J_dd) :
    ggh_sorting_swap_dH J_ll J_dd J_ld < 0 ∧
    ggh_hetero_surface_tension2 J_ll J_dd J_ld > 0 ∧
    ggh_sorting_swap_dH 14 2 11 = -6 ∧
    ggh_hetero_surface_tension2 14 2 11 = 6 ∧
    ggh_sorting_swap_dH J J J = 0 ∧
    ggh_hetero_surface_tension2 J J J = 0 := by
  unfold ggh_sorting_swap_dH ggh_hetero_surface_tension2; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "H = Σ_<ij> J(τ_i, τ_j)(1 - δ_{σ_i σ_j}) + λ_V Σ_σ (v_σ - V_T)^2;  2 J_ld > J_ll + J_dd ⟹ ΔH_swap = (J_ll + J_dd) - 2 J_ld < 0;  (14, 2, 11) ⟹ ΔH_swap = -6;  J_ll = J_dd = J_ld ⟹ ΔH_swap = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/aama.2001.0721>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0237>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2010.12.011>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.03.038>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2005.0033>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2004.2772>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1752-0509-1-16> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Multiscale Reactor-Mechanochemical Limb" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_014.ggh_sorting_swap_dH" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_014.ggh_differential_adhesion_sorting_condition" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Metropolis Haptotactic Acceptance in the Coupled GGH Cell Lattice (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the acceptance logic of the haptotaxis copy-energy term coupling the discrete cells to the continuum-derived fibronectin field: up-gradient extensions with sufficient haptotactic gain are accepted deterministically, and the anti-fibronectin ablation μ_F = 0 reduces the model to adhesion + volume dynamics (the da_only regime); the discrete counterpart of the continuum haptotactic flux law (Law 3) | Variables: F(x): cell-deposited fibronectin on the lattice (dF/dt = k_F c_a^+ R_2^disc - γ_F F); dF = F(target) - F(source) for a copy attempt; μ_F = 10 haptotaxis copy-energy strength; ΔH_adh, ΔH_vol: adhesion and volume-constraint energy changes; T = 10 Metropolis temperature" ;
    dct:source "Savill NJ, Hogeweg P (1997) J. Theor. Biol. 184(3):229-235 doi:10.1006/jtbi.1996.0237; Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL 69:2013 (Metropolis rule); Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. 271:372-387 (cell-fibronectin coupling)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py#L786-L824>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_014_tgfb_fibronectin_limb.lean#L166-L191> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ggh_total_dH (dH_adh dH_vol mu_F dF : Int) : Int := dH_adh + dH_vol - mu_F * dF
theorem ggh_metropolis_haptotaxis_acceptance (dH_adh dH_vol mu_F dF : Int)
    (hmu : mu_F ≥ 1) (hdF : dF ≥ 1) (hpen : dH_adh + dH_vol ≤ mu_F * dF) :
    ggh_total_dH dH_adh dH_vol mu_F dF ≤ 0 ∧
    ggh_total_dH dH_adh dH_vol 0 dF = dH_adh + dH_vol ∧
    ggh_total_dH dH_adh dH_vol mu_F dF < ggh_total_dH dH_adh dH_vol 0 dF := by
  unfold ggh_total_dH
  have hpos : mu_F * dF ≥ 1 * 1 := Int.mul_le_mul hmu hdF (by omega) (by omega)
  omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "ΔH = ΔH_adh + ΔH_vol - μ_F (F(target) - F(source));  P_accept = 1 if ΔH ≤ 0 else exp(-ΔH/T);  μ_F dF ≥ ΔH_adh + ΔH_vol ⟹ ΔH ≤ 0 (accepted w.p. 1);  μ_F = 0 ⟹ ΔH = ΔH_adh + ΔH_vol" ;
